// Which Unicode block a code point is in, and a block found by name, the
// way Java's `Character.UnicodeBlock` answers both.
//
// Held to OpenJDK 17 (Unicode 13): 308 blocks by code point, and every name
// `UnicodeBlock.forName` accepts. A block has up to three spellings -- the
// Java constant (`LATIN_1_SUPPLEMENT`), the Unicode name
// (`Latin-1 Supplement`) and that name without spaces -- compared without
// case, plus the names Java kept when Unicode renamed a block
// (`Combining Marks For Symbols`, `Cyrillic Supplementary`, `Greek`) and
// one alias no rule derives, `PHAGS-PA`.
// `SURROGATES_AREA` is found by name and never by code point, as in Java.
//
// The tables are written by scripts/lib/b47/gen_blocks.py from Java itself.

/// Block constant names with their spaced Unicode names, code point ranges,
/// and the one alias no rule derives.
type UbTable = { blocks: [(str, [str])], ranges: [(i64, i64, str)], keys: Map[str, str] }

